{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Elijah walked with Elisha by [Db]the river Jordan's [Ab]side
Ask me what you want, my son, before [Eb7]I cross the great divide
E[Ab]lisha said a double portion of [Db]your spirit let it [Ab]be
If you see me when I'm taken, it [Eb7]will come to you, said [Ab]he
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Swing low, chariot of [Db]fire
Horses of fire, carry him higher
[Ab]Up in a whirlwind, gone in a flash
[Eb7]Elijah went home and he never looked [Ab]back
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
As they walked along and talked, the [Db]sky began to [Ab]burn
A chariot came between them [Eb7]and there would be no return
[Ab]My father, oh my father, cried E[Db]lisha on the [Ab]ground
And he picked up the mantle that came [Eb7]floating softly [Ab]down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Swing low, chariot of [Db]fire
Horses of fire, carry him higher
[Ab]Up in a whirlwind, gone in a flash
E[Eb7]lijah went home and he never looked back
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Ab]He never looked back
No, he never looked back
{end_of_verse}
